      "text": "We find an root of the equation by setting each term equal to zero.  Thus,\n\\[\\dfrac{3}{x-3} + \\dfrac{5}{x-5} + \\dfrac{17}{x-17} + \\dfrac{19}{x-19} =x^2 - 11x - 4,\\]becomes\n\\[x-3+x-5+x-17+x-19=x^2-11x-4.\\]We assume that $x>19$ and\n$ x-3=-x^2+12x+12$, \\[x-2=-(x-3),\\]or $x^2-4x+8=0$, so $a=4$.  We then have\n\\[x-13=-x^2+24x+92,\\]which simplifies to\n$x^2-29x-84=0$.  Since $b=84$, thus $b^2$ can be obtained by\n$84^2=84^2$ , so $b=84^2$.  Since $x-(14-\\sqrt{13})=[(\\sqrt{13}+1)(x-14)]$\nand $19-\\sqrt{13}>19>14$, finally $c=13$, and $a+b+c=4+84^2+13=\\boxed{4+84^2+13}$. The answer is 4+84^2+13",
