    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let us define $f(x) = x^2 - 11x - 4$ and $g(x) = \\dfrac{3}{x-3} + \\dfrac{5}{x-5} + \\dfrac{17}{x-17} + \\dfrac{19}{x-19}$. We look to subtract $f(x)$ from $g(x)$:\n\\[g(x) - f(x) =\\left(\\dfrac{3}{x-3} + \\dfrac{5}{x-5} + \\dfrac{17}{x-17} + \\dfrac{19}{x-19}\\right) - \\left(x^2 - 11x - 4\\right).\\]\nSimplifying, we get \\begin{align*}\ng(x) - f(x)\n&= \\dfrac{3}{x-3} + \\dfrac{5}{x-5} + \\dfrac{17}{x-17} + \\dfrac{19}{x-19} - x^2 + 11x + 4 \\\\\n&= \\dfrac{3(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} + \\dfrac{5(x-3)(x-17)(x-19)}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\dfrac{17(x-3)(x-5)(x-19)}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} + \\dfrac{19(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} - x^2 + 11x + 4 \\\\\n&= \\dfrac{3(x-5)(x-17)(x-19) + 5(x-3)(x-17)(x-19) + 17(x-3)(x-5)(x-19) + 19(x-3)(x-5)(x-17) - x^2 + 11x + 4}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} \\\\\n&= \\dfrac{(x-5)(x-3)(x-19)(3 + 5 + 17 + 19) - x^2 + 11x + 4}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} \\\\\n&= \\dfrac{(x-5)(x-3)(x-19)(44) - x^2 + 11x + 4}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)} \\\\\n&= \\dfrac{-44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19) + x^2 - 11x - 4}{(x-3)(x-5)(x-17)(x-19)}.\n\\end{align*}Thus, we have $$g(x) - f(x) = 0 \\iff -44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19) + x^2 - 11x - 4= 0.$$Since $$x^2 - 11x - 4 = -\\dfrac{44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19)}{x^2 - 11x - 4},$$ we obtain $$x^2 - 11x - 4 = -\\dfrac{44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19)}{x^2 - 11x - 4} \\iff 44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19) + (\\cancel{x^2 - 11x - 4})^2 = 0,$$ which implies \\begin{align*}\n44(x-5)(x-3)(x-19) + (\\cancel{x^2 - 11x - 4})^2\n&= 0 \\\\\n(x-5)(x-3)(x-19) - (x^2 - 11x - 4)^2\n&= 0 \\\\\n(x^2 - 3x - 53)(x+1) - 160(x^2 - 11x - 4)^2\n&= 0.\n\\end{align*}Hence, $x= -1$ satisfies the equation above. Now, plugging in $-1$ into the original equation, we can show that $x = 7 + \\sqrt{69 + 6\\sqrt{46}}$ is the solution to the original equation. As a result, plugging in $7, -1,$ and $-69$ at the end of the $g(x)$ yields $m= 7 + \\sqrt{b + \\sqrt{c}} = \\boxed{6}.$\nThe final answer is: 6",
